       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day, so this is twice the limit.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg at once is also twice the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Risks:** At this level the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nTypical adult regimens are:\n- **Pain or inflammation:** 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours as needed, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Rheumatologic conditions:** 400\u2013800 mg PO three to four times daily, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n\nPossible intended orders include 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day). Tell me the dose and frequency you meant and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
